:- module(trho, [foo/2]).
:- use_module(library(prelude)).

% A rule head is an implementation site: its body must be correct at
% EVERY instantiation the store may hold, so the head allocates a
% rigid T. `X > Y` is overloaded, and no declared signature of `>` is
% consistent with a skolem — so the rule is rejected with
% NoMatchingOverload (spec §Soundness). Discharging it takes a
% `requiring` clause on the declaration (bounded_sorted_constraint)
% or an evidence guard that pins T
% (typecheck_rigid_head_evidence).
:- chr_constraint foo(T, T).

foo(X, Y) <=> X > Y.
